e right shape of diagnostic: it mirrors the matcher's filter order (worktree → SHA → window → AgentType), so the message tells the user the *first* check that would reject, which is the same one a developer would investigate first.\n- The handshake-rename fix (`\"gemini-cli\"` → `\"gemini\"` for the env-var payload) is a silent-failure repair — the kind that doesn't surface in tests unless you assert the registry key explicitly. The new `TestGeminiReviewer_NameMatchesRegistryKey` (and siblings for claude/codex) does exactly that. Lock-tests like this prevent regressions when contributors hardcode the name in new agents.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n### Findings\n\n**P1 — incomplete `gemini-cli` → `gemini` rename in test files**\n\nThe reviewer/registry now use `\"gemini\"`, but these still reference `\"gemini-cli\"`:\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker_test.go:227`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/dump_test.go:121, 156, 169, 170` — including assertions like `\"# gemini-cli review\"`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/run_test.go:260`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go:2600, 2629`\n\nSome are arbitrary fixture strings, but `dump_test.go:169-170` asserts the rendered heading, and that heading is now `\"# gemini review\"` in production. These will fail at runtime if not updated. The transcript-compact fixtures (`gemini_test.go`, `gemini_full.jsonl`, `gemini_expected.jsonl`) reasonably preserve `\"gemini-cli\"` as historical metadata — keep those as-is.\n\nAlso worth updating: `CLAUDE.md` mentions `\"gemini-cli\"` in agent-list copy in several places, and `agent_group.go:99` updated the help text but related help/examples may still reference the old key.\n\n**P1 — `.entire/settings.json` looks like a personal-config leak**\n\nThe working-tree change to `.entire/settings.json` adds review skill lists, a `review_fix_agent: \"claude-code\"`, `commit_linking: \"always\"`, and `summary_generation.model: \"sonnet\"`. If this is intended as a *project default* visible 